    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d609">

                <pb facs="0785" n="499" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2696</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Consul at Saloniki</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kehl</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-07-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 8, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department has not given its approval to arrangements for issuance [of] letters
                    of assurance by British Embassy, Washington. American consuls in Greece should
                    have nothing to do with requests of this character.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
